+## [2.0.0](https://github.com/rsionnach/nthlayer-workers/compare/v1.7.1...v2.0.0) (2026-08-28)
+
+
+### ⚠ BREAKING CHANGES
+
+* **observe:** observe.slo.spec_loader.load_specs now returns LoadedSpecs(service_slos, parse_failures) instead of list[ServiceSLO]. Callers iterating the return value directly must use `.service_slos`. The count exists so a caller can tell a partial view from a complete one: before this, a service whose manifest failed to parse contributed zero SLOs and was indistinguishable from one declaring none. Requires nthlayer-common>=2.1.2.
+* **measure:** three public shapes in `measure.adapters.prometheus` changed. `load_specs` now returns `LoadedSpecs(slos, parse_failures)` instead of `list[SLODefinition]` — note the field is `.slos`, NOT `.service_slos` as in observe's separate `LoadedSpecs`; the two are different classes and a migration that assumes one shape will `AttributeError` on the other. `SLODefinition` gains a required `query_kind` field and `EvaluationResult` a required `raw_breach`, so any code constructing either directly now raises `TypeError` until updated. `query_kind` is deliberately defaultless: it selects the breach rule (`judgment_rate` inverts a 0-1 rate to an SLI, `ratio` scales without inverting, `latency_seconds` and `judgment_duration` compare durations, `error_budget` tests a signed budget against zero), and a wrong default would evaluate, write a verdict, and simply be wrong. Also behavioural: judgment hysteresis now counts each window's stored `raw_breach`, so verdicts written by 1.x carry none and stop the count — expect one restarted hysteresis window per judgment SLO on upgrade, rather than a guess at their state. `evaluate-once --hysteresis` below 1 now exits 2. Requires nthlayer-common>=2.1.2.
+
