-## Conventions
-
-- Each worker module exposes its own `cli.py` with a `main()` function and is invoked via `uv run --directory nthlayer-workers`
-- Top-level `nthlayer-workers serve` starts all registered modules; observe split into three modules (ObserveCollectModule/ObserveDriftModule/ObserveTopologyModule) as of P3-B.2; correlate split into three modules (CorrelateSessionModule/CorrelateTopologyModule/CorrelateContractModule) as of P3-D.2; MeasureModule implemented [P3-C.1]; RespondModule implemented [P3-E.1] — structural migration complete (I/O → core API, CLI → poll-driven, SQLiteVerdictStore/SQLiteContextStore removed from worker path); P3-E.2 (Instructor), P3-E.3 (approval-verdict poll+resume), P3-E.4 (notifications), P3-E.5 (on-call) are follow-up beads; learn: LearnOutcomeModule (60s) + LearnRetrospectiveModule (30s) implemented [P3-F.1]; recommendations module (Learn → Spec feedback loop foundation) added [opensrm-jmy.2] — full --apply-to / --pr / spec patch generation deferred to opensrm-jmy.6
-- One module = one responsibility; no internal timers — use separate module registrations at different intervals instead
-- Never access nthlayer-core SQLite store directly — all reads/writes go through `CoreAPIClient` HTTP API
-- Verdict data model lives in `nthlayer_common.verdicts`; learn module only adds analytical operations on top
